{"id":"ch-fig-004","s":"chem","t":"3.1.5","lv":2,"q":"Experiments X and Y react the same mass of magnesium with excess acid at different temperatures. Use points P and Q to find how many times greater the average rate of X is than Y over the first 20 s.","o":["20","2","40","0.5"],"a":1,"x":"Average rate = volume ÷ time. X reaches 40 cm³ at P and Y reaches 20 cm³ at Q, both in 20 s. The rates are 2.0 and 1.0 cm³/s, so X is 2 times faster (40 ÷ 20).","w":["Subtracts the volumes (40 − 20) instead of dividing them. The question asks for a ratio of rates, not a difference in volume.","","Gives the volume read at P rather than comparing the two rates. A ratio needs both curves, divided one by the other.","Divides the wrong way round (Y ÷ X). X is the steeper curve, so its rate is the larger and the ratio must be above 1."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,80],"y":[0,60],"xstep":10,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"volume of H₂ / cm³","xnums":true,"ynums":true,"lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.5,1.625494],[1.0,3.206951],[1.5,4.745563],[2.0,6.242492],[2.5,7.698867],[3.0,9.115787],[3.5,10.49432],[4.0,11.835506],[4.5,13.140358],[5.0,14.409859],[5.5,15.644967],[6.0,16.846614],[6.5,18.015707],[7.0,19.153127],[7.5,20.259733],[8.0,21.336359],[8.5,22.383818],[9.0,23.402899],[9.5,24.394372],[10.0,25.358984],[10.5,26.297463],[11.0,27.210518],[11.5,28.098836],[12.0,28.963089],[12.5,29.803927],[13.0,30.621986],[13.5,31.417882],[14.0,32.192217],[14.5,32.945573],[15.0,33.67852],[15.5,34.39161],[16.0,35.085381],[16.5,35.760357],[17.0,36.417047],[17.5,37.055946],[18.0,37.677537],[18.5,38.282287],[19.0,38.870654],[19.5,39.443081],[20.0,40.0],[20.5,40.541831],[21.0,41.068984],[21.5,41.581854],[22.0,42.080831],[22.5,42.566289],[23.0,43.038596],[23.5,43.498107],[24.0,43.945169],[24.5,44.380119],[25.0,44.803286],[25.5,45.214989],[26.0,45.615538],[26.5,46.005236],[27.0,46.384376],[27.5,46.753244],[28.0,47.11212],[28.5,47.461273],[29.0,47.800966],[29.5,48.131457],[30.0,48.452995],[30.5,48.765821]